  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\n(1st number + 2nd number)2 = 3rd number.\n\nNow,\n\n(2, 4, 36)\n\n⇒ (2 + 4)2 → 62 = 36\n\nFor (4, 6, 100)\n\n⇒ (4 + 6)2 → 102 = 100.\n\nNow, checking the options:\n\nOption 1: (8, 4, 1020)\n\n⇒ (8 + 4)² → 122 =144 ≠ 1020.\n\nOption 2: (12, 4, 230)\n\n⇒ (12 + 4)2 → 162 = 256 ≠ 230.\n\n**Option 3: (4, 4, 64)**\n\n**⇒ (4 + 4)2 → 82 = 64 = 64.**\n\nOption 4: (14, 2, 75)\n\n⇒ (14 + 2)2 → 162 = 256 ≠ 75.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option 3\".",
